From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: S905L3 local bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: meson-gx: allow limiting request blocks

Some board/card combinations enumerate correctly but fail larger descriptor
transfers during early block probing. Add a Meson-specific DT knob that clamps
the host request size before mmc_add_host(), so the block queue is constrained
before mmcblk probes for partition metadata.

This is intended as a board quirk, not a replacement for normal timing
configuration.

Signed-off-by: S905L3 local bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 .../bindings/mmc/amlogic,meson-gx-mmc.yaml   | 10 ++++++++++
 drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c              | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/amlogic,meson-gx-mmc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/amlogic,meson-gx-mmc.yaml
index 12196184b..9fc1b8c33 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/amlogic,meson-gx-mmc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/amlogic,meson-gx-mmc.yaml
@@ -50,6 +50,16 @@ properties:
       set when controller's internal DMA engine cannot access the DRAM memory,
       like on the G12A dedicated SDIO controller.
 
+  amlogic,max-request-blocks:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    minimum: 1
+    maximum: 511
+    description:
+      Maximum number of blocks in one request. This is a board-specific
+      fallback for card/controller combinations that enumerate correctly but
+      fail larger descriptor transfers during early block probing. The Meson
+      GX command length field supports up to 511 blocks.
+
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c
index 3376759f6..6e83a0ecf 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c
@@ -1147,7 +1147,8 @@ static int meson_mmc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct meson_host *host;
 	struct mmc_host *mmc;
 	struct clk *core_clk;
-	int cd_irq, ret;
+	u32 max_request_blocks;
+	int cd_irq, ret;
 
 	mmc = devm_mmc_alloc_host(&pdev->dev, sizeof(struct meson_host));
 	if (!mmc)
@@ -1239,6 +1240,14 @@ static int meson_mmc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		mmc->max_segs = SD_EMMC_DESC_BUF_LEN /
 				sizeof(struct sd_emmc_desc);
 	}
+	if (!device_property_read_u32(&pdev->dev, "amlogic,max-request-blocks",
+				      &max_request_blocks)) {
+		if (!max_request_blocks)
+			return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -EINVAL,
+					     "invalid amlogic,max-request-blocks\n");
+		mmc->max_blk_count = min_t(unsigned int, mmc->max_blk_count,
+					   max_request_blocks);
+	}
 	mmc->max_req_size = mmc->max_blk_count * mmc->max_blk_size;
 	mmc->max_seg_size = mmc->max_req_size;
 
-- 
